  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Australian Patience. Type: Solitaire (Scorpion/Klondike mix). Rules: 52 cards. Build down in suit. Any card and its stack can be moved. Stock is 1-by-1, no redeals. Goal: 4 foundations A-K.',
    Player: "Welcome to Australian Patience! Unlike Klondike, you must build down in the SAME suit. Every card on the table is visible, so take a moment to find your Aces. Remember, once the stock is gone, you're on your own!",
    objective: 'Move all 52 cards to the four foundation piles, organized by suit from Ace to King.',
    gameplay: '1. Deal: 7 columns of 4 cards each, face-up (28 cards). Stock = 24 cards. 2. Play: Build tableau down in suit only. Move cards (and any cards on top) to other columns or to foundations. Flip stock one at a time to waste; top of waste is playable. 3. Foundations: Aces up in suit (A-2-3...K). 4. Win when all 52 cards are on foundations.',
    keyRules: [
      "Suit Building: You MUST follow suit in the tableau (unlike Klondike's alternating colors).",
      'Visibility: All 28 starting cards are visible; use this to plan 3-4 moves ahead.',
      'No Redeal: If the stock is empty and no moves remain, the game is lost.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'One player for the standard solitaire game. The player shuffles and deals their own tableau; there is no dealer or opponent. Australian Patience can also be played competitively by two players (each with their own 52-card pack and tableau), but the primary form documented here is single-player.',
      deck: 'Standard 52 cards (Aces low).',
      equipment: 'Standard pack, ample table surface.',
      dealing: '7 columns of 4 cards are dealt face-up, slightly overlapped. This uses 28 cards. The remaining 24 cards form the draw pile (stock).',
    },
    turnFlow: '1. Deal: 7 columns of 4 cards each, face-up (28 cards). Stock = 24 cards. 2. Play: Build tableau down in suit only. Move cards (and any cards on top) to other columns or to foundations. Flip stock one at a time to waste; top of waste is playable. 3. Foundations: Aces up in suit (A-2-3...K). 4. Win when all 52 cards are on foundations.',
